  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_029: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat → 0.629 acc), so evidence is extremely sparse and the most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes. Config_003 (RNA-only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_029: it removes only the image modality while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical. If RNA-only performs comparably, the image modality is not adding value and the search should pivot toward RNA-encoder and aggregation choices; if it is substantially worse, multimodal fusion is confirmed as worthwhile and we can exploit that direction. Establishing this modality baseline before further multimodal variants is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a limited budget, because it determines whether the entire fusion/aggregation design space is worth exploring."
}

